  "readings": [
    "the primary completes 128/128 development and 128/128 on fresh final worlds with 128/128 correct depths, emitting a decoded answer token for every request",
    "freezing the learned relation match, freezing continuation to always-continue, and disabling reads each drop the complete answers to 0/128, so relation discrimination, content-dependent continuation and reading are each necessary",
    "removing exactly the required record makes the session stop explicitly unresolved with no emission in 16/16 worlds, and a learned compatibility gate is what distinguishes a missing fact from an incompatible one",
    "a single-position source edit changes the first retained value, the follow-up relation query, the selected second occurrence and the final answer together, matching the independently derived expectation; changing only the request relation changes the selected fact and the answer while all records stay fixed",
    "an added plausible distractor with the same key and an unseen role preserves both the answer and the selected roles",
    "pause/resume is identical on 128/128 requests, two interleaved frames stay independent, and an owned captured payload remains usable after its origin was overwritten while the separate origin liveness check reports false",
    "the matched categorical and cyclic controls reach the same 128/128, so this task establishes learned relational access and control, not geometric advantage"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "supplied token layout, record triples and follow-up convention; only the role/relation correspondence, the ranking and the continuation decision are learned",
